@@ -23,3 +23,4 @@ Refresh the patch against the new upstream, or drop it once upstream has the fix
 | Patch | Why |
 |---|---|
 | `0001-jaza-empty-answer.patch` | `jaza()` treated an empty answer or the typed word `null` as a failure in the browser, while the stdin replay path accepted them. Only a JS `null`/`undefined` from `prompt()` (no input available, or the run was stopped) is a failure now. |
+| `0002-division-by-zero.patch` | `/`, `%` and `/=` with a zero divisor returned Go's `+Inf` or `NaN` as the answer, and integer `%` or `/=` crashed the run with a Go panic. All of them now stop the program with `Kosa: Mstari N: Huwezi kugawanya kwa sifuri`. |
